<!-- ==================== SECTION 1 ==================== -->
<div class="page-break"></div>
<h2>1. Title of the Project</h2>
<p><b style="font-size:14pt; color:#1a1a2e;">Online Shoes Selling System</b></p>
<p>The Online Shoes Selling System is a comprehensive web-based e-commerce platform designed to facilitate the buying and selling of footwear products through the internet. The system provides a seamless shopping experience for customers, efficient product and order management capabilities for administrators, and intelligent inventory tracking for inventory staff. The platform integrates smart features like AI-based product recommendations, automated email notifications using n8n workflow automation, and a responsive user interface to deliver a modern, industry-standard online shoe store.</p>

<!-- ==================== SECTION 2 ==================== -->
<h2>2. Stakeholders Involved in Capturing Requirements</h2>
<p>The following stakeholders were involved in the process of capturing and analyzing the requirements for the Online Shoes Selling System:</p>
<table>
  <thead>
    <tr>
      <th style="width:5%;">Sr. No.</th>
      <th style="width:30%;">Stakeholder</th>
      <th>Role / Involvement</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr><td>1</td><td>Shoe Store Owner</td><td>Primary client who defined business rules, product catalog requirements, pricing strategy, and sales goals for the online platform.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>2</td><td>Customers (End Users)</td><td>Provided feedback on shopping experience expectations, UI preferences, search/filter requirements, and checkout flow needs.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>3</td><td>Administrator</td><td>Specified requirements for managing products, orders, users, coupons, returns, reports, and overall system configuration.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>4</td><td>Inventory Manager</td><td>Defined requirements for stock management, low-stock alerts, inventory reports, and product availability tracking.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>5</td><td>Sales Manager</td><td>Provided input on sales analytics, coupon/discount management, revenue reporting, and promotional features.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>6</td><td>Delivery Partner</td><td>Shared requirements regarding order dispatch workflow, delivery tracking, and shipment status updates.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>7</td><td>Marketing Team</td><td>Defined requirements for email campaigns, promotional banners, abandoned cart reminders, and customer engagement automation.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>8</td><td>Project Guide (Faculty)</td><td>Supervised the requirement gathering process, provided academic guidance, and validated the scope of the project.</td></tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

<!-- ==================== SECTION 3 ==================== -->
<h2>3. Techniques Used for Requirement Capturing</h2>
<p>The following techniques were employed to gather, analyze, and validate the requirements for the system:</p>
<table>
  <thead>
    <tr>
      <th style="width:5%;">Sr. No.</th>
      <th style="width:28%;">Technique</th>
      <th>Description</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr><td>1</td><td>Interviews</td><td>One-on-one interviews were conducted with the shoe store owner and sales manager to understand business workflows, product catalog structure, pricing models, and customer service expectations.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>2</td><td>Questionnaires &amp; Surveys</td><td>Online surveys were distributed among potential customers to gather preferences regarding shoe shopping habits, preferred payment methods, filter/search expectations, and UI design preferences.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>3</td><td>Observation</td><td>Existing online shoe stores (such as Nike, Adidas, Myntra, Flipkart Shoes section) were observed and analyzed to understand industry-standard features, user flows, and best practices in e-commerce.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>4</td><td>Market Research</td><td>Market analysis was conducted to identify trending features in online shoe retail, including AI-based recommendations, virtual try-on concepts, size prediction, and personalized shopping experiences.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>5</td><td>Brainstorming Sessions</td><td>Team brainstorming sessions were held to generate innovative feature ideas such as smart inventory alerts, automated email workflows using n8n, and AI-powered product suggestions.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>6</td><td>Competitor Analysis</td><td>Competitor platforms were analyzed to benchmark features, identify gaps, and ensure the system offers competitive advantages in terms of functionality, UI/UX, and automation.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>7</td><td>Requirement Analysis Meetings</td><td>Regular meetings were conducted with the project guide and team members to review, refine, prioritize, and finalize the gathered requirements before documentation.</td></tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

