<!-- ==================== SECTION 6 ==================== -->
<h2>6. Users of the System</h2>
<p>The Online Shoes Selling System is designed to serve the following types of users:</p>
<table>
  <thead>
    <tr>
      <th style="width:5%;">Sr. No.</th>
      <th style="width:22%;">User Type</th>
      <th>Description &amp; Access Level</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr><td>1</td><td><b>Guest User</b></td><td>Can browse shoes, view product details, search and filter products. Cannot add items to cart, place orders, or write reviews until they register.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>2</td><td><b>Registered Customer</b></td><td>Full access to shopping features including cart, wishlist, checkout, order placement, order tracking, address management, product reviews &amp; ratings, return requests, and invoice downloads.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>3</td><td><b>Administrator</b></td><td>Full backend access to manage products, categories, brands, product images, orders, returns, customers, coupons, discounts, reports, analytics dashboard, notifications, and system settings.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>4</td><td><b>Inventory Manager</b></td><td>Access to stock management features including adding/updating/deleting stock, monitoring inventory levels, receiving low-stock alerts, generating inventory reports, and tracking stock history.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>5</td><td><b>Sales Staff</b></td><td>Access to view orders, process order status updates, view sales reports, and manage day-to-day sales operations.</td></tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

<!-- ==================== SECTION 7 ==================== -->
<div class="page-break"></div>
<h2>7. Consolidated List of Initial Requirements</h2>
<p>The following is the comprehensive list of all functional requirements captured for the Online Shoes Selling System, categorized by user module:</p>

<!-- 7.1 Customer Requirements -->
<h3>7.1 Customer Module Requirements</h3>
<table>
  <thead>
    <tr>
      <th style="width:10%;">Req. ID</th>
      <th style="width:28%;">Requirement</th>
      <th>Description</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr><td class="req-id">CR-001</td><td>User Registration</td><td>Customers can create a new account by providing name, email, phone number, and password. Email verification shall be sent upon registration.</td></tr>
    <tr><td class="req-id">CR-002</td><td>User Login / Logout</td><td>Registered customers can securely log in using email and password, and log out from any page. Session management ensures security.</td></tr>
    <tr><td class="req-id">CR-003</td><td>Forgot Password</td><td>Customers can reset their password through an email-based password recovery link sent to their registered email address.</td></tr>
    <tr><td class="req-id">CR-004</td><td>Email Verification</td><td>A verification email is sent upon registration. Account activation requires the customer to verify their email address.</td></tr>
    <tr><td class="req-id">CR-005</td><td>Browse Shoes</td><td>Customers can browse through the entire shoe catalog with pagination. Products are displayed with images, names, prices, and ratings.</td></tr>
    <tr><td class="req-id">CR-006</td><td>Search Shoes</td><td>A search bar allows customers to search products by name, brand, category, or keywords with instant search suggestions.</td></tr>
    <tr><td class="req-id">CR-007</td><td>Filter by Brand</td><td>Customers can filter products by selecting one or more shoe brands (e.g., Nike, Adidas, Puma, Reebok, etc.).</td></tr>
    <tr><td class="req-id">CR-008</td><td>Filter by Size</td><td>Customers can filter available shoes by selecting their preferred shoe size (e.g., 6, 7, 8, 9, 10, 11, 12).</td></tr>
    <tr><td class="req-id">CR-009</td><td>Filter by Color</td><td>Products can be filtered based on available color options (e.g., Black, White, Red, Blue, Multi-color).</td></tr>
    <tr><td class="req-id">CR-010</td><td>Filter by Price Range</td><td>A price range slider or input allows customers to filter shoes within a minimum and maximum price range.</td></tr>
    <tr><td class="req-id">CR-011</td><td>Filter by Category</td><td>Customers can browse shoes by categories such as Running, Casual, Formal, Sports, Sandals, Loafers, Boots, etc.</td></tr>
    <tr><td class="req-id">CR-012</td><td>View Product Details</td><td>Clicking on a product shows full details including multiple images, description, available sizes, colors, stock status, ratings, and reviews.</td></tr>
    <tr><td class="req-id">CR-013</td><td>View Product Images</td><td>Product detail page displays multiple high-quality images with zoom and thumbnail navigation.</td></tr>
    <tr><td class="req-id">CR-014</td><td>Add to Wishlist</td><td>Registered customers can add products to their wishlist for future purchase consideration.</td></tr>
    <tr><td class="req-id">CR-015</td><td>Remove from Wishlist</td><td>Customers can remove previously added items from their wishlist.</td></tr>
    <tr><td class="req-id">CR-016</td><td>Add to Cart</td><td>Customers can add products to their shopping cart with selected size, color, and quantity.</td></tr>
    <tr><td class="req-id">CR-017</td><td>Update Cart</td><td>Customers can modify the quantity of items in their cart or change selected size/color options.</td></tr>
    <tr><td class="req-id">CR-018</td><td>Remove Items from Cart</td><td>Customers can delete individual items from their shopping cart.</td></tr>
    <tr><td class="req-id">CR-019</td><td>Secure Checkout</td><td>A multi-step checkout process collects shipping address, selects payment method, applies coupons, and confirms the order.</td></tr>
    <tr><td class="req-id">CR-020</td><td>Address Management</td><td>Customers can add, edit, and delete multiple shipping addresses. A default address can be set for quick checkout.</td></tr>
    <tr><td class="req-id">CR-021</td><td>Order Placement</td><td>After checkout, the order is confirmed and an order confirmation page is displayed with the order summary and estimated delivery date.</td></tr>
    <tr><td class="req-id">CR-022</td><td>Order Tracking</td><td>Customers can track their orders in real-time with status updates (Confirmed, Packed, Shipped, Out for Delivery, Delivered).</td></tr>
    <tr><td class="req-id">CR-023</td><td>Order History</td><td>A complete history of all past orders is available with details, invoice download option, and reorder functionality.</td></tr>
    <tr><td class="req-id">CR-024</td><td>Product Reviews</td><td>Customers can write text reviews for purchased products to share their experience.</td></tr>
    <tr><td class="req-id">CR-025</td><td>Product Ratings</td><td>Customers can rate purchased products on a 1-to-5 star scale. Average rating is displayed on product cards.</td></tr>
    <tr><td class="req-id">CR-026</td><td>Return Request</td><td>Customers can initiate return requests for eligible orders within the return window with a reason for return.</td></tr>
    <tr><td class="req-id">CR-027</td><td>Invoice Download</td><td>Customers can download PDF invoices for their completed orders from the order history section.</td></tr>
    <tr><td class="req-id">CR-028</td><td>Order Status Notifications</td><td>Automated email/SMS notifications are sent to customers when order status changes (confirmed, shipped, delivered, etc.).</td></tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

<!-- 7.2 Administrator Requirements -->
<div class="page-break"></div>
<h3>7.2 Administrator Module Requirements</h3>
<table>
  <thead>
    <tr>
      <th style="width:10%;">Req. ID</th>
      <th style="width:28%;">Requirement</th>
      <th>Description</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr><td class="req-id">AR-001</td><td>Admin Login</td><td>Administrators can securely log in to the admin panel using credentials with role-based access control.</td></tr>
    <tr><td class="req-id">AR-002</td><td>Manage Customers</td><td>Admin can view, search, activate, deactivate, and delete customer accounts. Customer order history and profile details are accessible.</td></tr>
    <tr><td class="req-id">AR-003</td><td>Manage Products</td><td>Admin can add new shoes, edit existing product details (name, description, price, brand, category), and delete products from the catalog.</td></tr>
    <tr><td class="req-id">AR-004</td><td>Manage Categories</td><td>Admin can create, edit, and delete product categories (e.g., Running, Casual, Formal, Sports, Boots, Sandals).</td></tr>
    <tr><td class="req-id">AR-005</td><td>Manage Brands</td><td>Admin can add, edit, and remove shoe brands (e.g., Nike, Adidas, Puma, Reebok, New Balance, etc.).</td></tr>
    <tr><td class="req-id">AR-006</td><td>Manage Product Images</td><td>Admin can upload, reorder, and delete multiple images for each product. Image optimization is handled automatically.</td></tr>
    <tr><td class="req-id">AR-007</td><td>Manage Product Variants</td><td>Admin can define size and color variants for each product with individual stock levels and pricing.</td></tr>
    <tr><td class="req-id">AR-008</td><td>Manage Inventory</td><td>Admin can view overall inventory status, update stock quantities, and set low-stock threshold values for alerts.</td></tr>
    <tr><td class="req-id">AR-009</td><td>Manage Orders</td><td>Admin can view all orders, update order status (Processing, Packed, Shipped, Delivered, Cancelled), and add tracking information.</td></tr>
    <tr><td class="req-id">AR-010</td><td>Manage Returns</td><td>Admin can review return requests, approve or reject returns, process refunds, and update return status.</td></tr>
    <tr><td class="req-id">AR-011</td><td>Manage Coupons</td><td>Admin can create, edit, activate, deactivate, and delete discount coupons with configurable parameters (percentage/flat, min order, expiry date, usage limit).</td></tr>
    <tr><td class="req-id">AR-012</td><td>Manage Discounts</td><td>Admin can set product-level or category-level discount percentages and schedule sale events with start and end dates.</td></tr>
    <tr><td class="req-id">AR-013</td><td>Generate Reports</td><td>Admin can generate reports for sales, revenue, orders, inventory, customer registrations, and product performance with date range filters.</td></tr>
    <tr><td class="req-id">AR-014</td><td>View Sales Analytics</td><td>A visual dashboard displays real-time analytics including revenue trends, top-selling products, order volume, and conversion rates.</td></tr>
    <tr><td class="req-id">AR-015</td><td>Send Notifications</td><td>Admin can send email notifications to individual customers or broadcast announcements to all users regarding offers, new arrivals, or order updates.</td></tr>
    <tr><td class="req-id">AR-016</td><td>Manage User Accounts</td><td>Admin can create additional admin or staff accounts with role-based permissions to delegate backend responsibilities.</td></tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

<!-- 7.3 Inventory Management Requirements -->
<h3>7.3 Inventory Management Module Requirements</h3>
<table>
  <thead>
    <tr>
      <th style="width:10%;">Req. ID</th>
      <th style="width:28%;">Requirement</th>
      <th>Description</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr><td class="req-id">IR-001</td><td>Add Stock</td><td>Inventory manager can add new stock entries specifying product, size, color, quantity, supplier, and batch details.</td></tr>
    <tr><td class="req-id">IR-002</td><td>Update Stock</td><td>Existing stock quantities can be updated (incremented or decremented) with reason logging for audit purposes.</td></tr>
    <tr><td class="req-id">IR-003</td><td>Delete Stock</td><td>Discontinued or damaged stock entries can be removed from the inventory with proper documentation.</td></tr>
    <tr><td class="req-id">IR-004</td><td>Low Stock Alerts</td><td>The system automatically generates alerts when stock quantity falls below the configured threshold. Alerts are shown on the dashboard and sent via email.</td></tr>
    <tr><td class="req-id">IR-005</td><td>Inventory Reports</td><td>Detailed inventory reports can be generated showing current stock levels, stock movement history, sell-through rates, and dead stock analysis.</td></tr>
    <tr><td class="req-id">IR-006</td><td>Stock History</td><td>A complete audit trail of all stock changes is maintained with timestamps, user details, quantities changed, and reasons.</td></tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

<!-- 7.4 Payment Requirements -->
<div class="page-break"></div>
<h3>7.4 Payment Module Requirements</h3>
<table>
  <thead>
    <tr>
      <th style="width:10%;">Req. ID</th>
      <th style="width:28%;">Requirement</th>
      <th>Description</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr><td class="req-id">PR-001</td><td>Cash on Delivery (COD)</td><td>Customers can choose to pay in cash at the time of delivery. COD availability may be restricted based on order value or location.</td></tr>
    <tr><td class="req-id">PR-002</td><td>UPI Payment</td><td>Integration with UPI payment gateways (Google Pay, PhonePe, Paytm) for instant digital payments.</td></tr>
    <tr><td class="req-id">PR-003</td><td>Credit/Debit Card Payment</td><td>Secure card payment processing through payment gateway integration with PCI-DSS compliance.</td></tr>
    <tr><td class="req-id">PR-004</td><td>Online Payment Confirmation</td><td>Upon successful online payment, a confirmation page is displayed and a payment receipt is sent via email to the customer.</td></tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

<!-- ==================== SECTION 8 ==================== -->
<h2>8. Non-Functional Requirements</h2>
<p>The following non-functional requirements define the quality attributes and constraints of the Online Shoes Selling System:</p>
<table>
  <thead>
    <tr>
      <th style="width:5%;">Sr. No.</th>
      <th style="width:25%;">Requirement</th>
      <th>Description</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr><td>1</td><td>Fast System Response</td><td>All pages shall load within 3 seconds under normal network conditions. Database queries shall be optimized for performance.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>2</td><td>Secure Authentication</td><td>User authentication shall use secure hashing algorithms (bcrypt/SHA-256) for passwords. Session tokens shall be used for maintaining login state.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>3</td><td>Password Encryption</td><td>All user passwords shall be stored in encrypted/hashed format in the database. Plain-text passwords shall never be stored.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>4</td><td>Data Backup</td><td>Regular automated database backups shall be configured to prevent data loss. Backup frequency: daily.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>5</td><td>High Availability</td><td>The system shall maintain 99% uptime. Error handling shall ensure graceful degradation without data loss.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>6</td><td>Scalability</td><td>The system architecture shall support horizontal scaling to handle increased user load and product catalog growth.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>7</td><td>Mobile Responsive Design</td><td>The UI shall be fully responsive across all screen sizes — desktop, tablet, and mobile devices using CSS media queries.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>8</td><td>Cross-Browser Compatibility</td><td>The application shall work consistently across all major browsers: Chrome, Firefox, Safari, Edge, and Opera.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>9</td><td>User-Friendly Interface</td><td>The UI shall follow modern design principles with intuitive navigation, clear typography, consistent color scheme, and accessible design.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>10</td><td>Reliable Performance</td><td>The system shall handle at least 500 concurrent users without performance degradation.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>11</td><td>Error Logging</td><td>All system errors and exceptions shall be logged with timestamps, error details, and stack traces for debugging purposes.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>12</td><td>Data Recovery</td><td>In case of system failure, data shall be recoverable from the latest backup with minimal data loss (RPO: 24 hours).</td></tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

<!-- ==================== SECTION 9 ==================== -->
<div class="page-break"></div>
<h2>9. Technology Stack</h2>
<p>The Online Shoes Selling System shall be developed using the following technologies:</p>
<table>
  <thead>
    <tr>
      <th style="width:20%;">Layer</th>
      <th style="width:25%;">Technology</th>
      <th>Purpose</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr><td><b>Frontend</b></td><td>HTML5</td><td>Structuring web pages with semantic markup for accessibility and SEO.</td></tr>
    <tr><td></td><td>CSS3</td><td>Styling and responsive design using Flexbox, Grid, media queries, animations, and glassmorphism effects.</td></tr>
    <tr><td></td><td>JavaScript (Vanilla)</td><td>Client-side interactivity, DOM manipulation, form validation, dynamic content rendering, and AJAX calls.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><b>Backend</b></td><td>PHP</td><td>Server-side logic, API development, database operations, session management, authentication, and business logic implementation.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><b>Database</b></td><td>MySQL</td><td>Relational database for storing users, products, orders, inventory, reviews, and all application data.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><b>Automation</b></td><td>n8n (Workflow Automation)</td><td>Automating email notifications (order confirmation, invoice, abandoned cart reminders, review reminders), scheduled reports, and webhook-based integrations.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><b>Web Server</b></td><td>Apache (XAMPP/WAMP)</td><td>Local development server for hosting PHP application and MySQL database.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><b>Version Control</b></td><td>Git &amp; GitHub</td><td>Source code version control, collaboration, and project repository management.</td></tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

<div class="note-box">
  <b>Note on n8n Automation:</b> n8n is an open-source workflow automation tool that will be used to create automated email workflows triggered by system events such as order placement, shipment updates, abandoned carts, and weekly sales report generation. n8n connects with the PHP backend via webhooks and APIs.
</div>

<!-- ==================== SECTION 10 ==================== -->
<h2>10. Future Enhancements</h2>
<p>The following features are identified as potential future enhancements to extend the capabilities of the Online Shoes Selling System beyond the initial release:</p>
<table>
  <thead>
    <tr>
      <th style="width:5%;">Sr. No.</th>
      <th style="width:30%;">Enhancement</th>
      <th>Description</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr><td>1</td><td>AI Product Recommendations</td><td>Machine learning-based product recommendation engine suggesting shoes based on browsing history, purchase patterns, and user preferences.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>2</td><td>Personalized Product Suggestions</td><td>Personalized homepage and product listing based on individual customer behavior and demographic data.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>3</td><td>Recently Viewed Products</td><td>Display a section showing products the customer has recently viewed for quick access and re-engagement.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>4</td><td>Frequently Bought Together</td><td>Show product bundles that are commonly purchased together to increase average order value.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>5</td><td>Chatbot / Live Chat Support</td><td>AI-powered chatbot for instant customer support, order inquiries, size recommendations, and FAQ responses.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>6</td><td>Email Notifications (via n8n)</td><td>Automated email campaigns for order confirmation, shipping updates, delivery confirmation, review requests, and promotional offers.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>7</td><td>SMS Notifications</td><td>SMS alerts for order status updates, OTP verification, and promotional messages via SMS gateway integration.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>8</td><td>Abandoned Cart Reminder</td><td>Automated email/notification sent to customers who added items to cart but did not complete the purchase within a specified time.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>9</td><td>Sales Analytics Dashboard</td><td>Advanced business intelligence dashboard with charts, graphs, and KPIs for data-driven decision making.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>10</td><td>Loyalty Reward System</td><td>Points-based loyalty program where customers earn points on purchases and can redeem them for discounts on future orders.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>11</td><td>Mobile Application</td><td>Native Android and iOS mobile applications for an enhanced mobile shopping experience with push notifications.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>12</td><td>Voice Search</td><td>Voice-based product search functionality using Web Speech API for hands-free product discovery.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>13</td><td>QR Code Order Tracking</td><td>Generate QR codes for each order that customers can scan to instantly view real-time delivery status.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>14</td><td>Multi-Language Support</td><td>Internationalization (i18n) support to serve customers in multiple languages for a wider audience reach.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>15</td><td>Compare Shoes</td><td>Side-by-side product comparison feature allowing customers to compare specifications, prices, and reviews of multiple shoes.</td></tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

